clothes rooted in hip-hop damon felt  that he could appeal to his younger self  and give modern kids what he never had  and with that damon founded for us bias  or fubu in 1992  damond barely had any money himself but  his mother would pull through and risk  it all for damond she mortgaged her  house and lent him 100 000 to start up  their business  mistakes couldn't have been higher but  this was damon's one shot at a better  life and there was no way he was going  to give that up  from the very beginning damien knew that  the key to growing a large clothing  brand was exposure but he decided to  start small and keep things simple  daemon continued to produce the wool  hats that had already sold well and he  continued working as a waiter in the  meantime he started experimenting with  sewing screen printed t-shirts  as the hat business grew damond hired  two of his childhood friends to start  selling t-shirts around the neighborhood  this worked out decently well at the  beginning but selling clothes  door-to-door clearly wasn't a very good  sales channel long term so damon started  leveraging consignments a consignment is  simply an agreement with a store or  vendor to sell your products for a set  commission or fee damond was able to  score a couple of consignment deals with  vendors in the northeast and with that  they many could start focusing on  actually building a brand damond and his  friends started selling the fubu logo  into hockey jerseys sweatshirts and  t-shirts and they lent out this clothing  to up-and-coming rappers to use in their  music videos within just two years  demand was able to secure product  placement within 30 music videos which  gave fubu quite a bit of exposure people  watching these music videos thought that  fubu was a decently sized small brand  but really it was just damond and a  couple of his friends and this became  painfully apparent when fubu started to  receive their first big orders in the  early 1990s damon traveled to las vegas  to showcase fubu at a fashion trade show  called magic this was definitely a  worthwhile trip given that he received  three hundred thousand dollars worth of  orders and an offer to be sold at select  macy's outlets damon had played took the  orders but only he knew that it was  going to be a massive struggle to  produce that many clothes as soon as he  returned home damon applied for loans at  every bank he could think of but he was  rejected from all 27 banks he applied to  so in a last-ditch effort damon used the  last of his money to put out an  advertisement in the new york times  looking for a manufacturing partner and  luckily for day mended samsung textiles  responded to the ad and helped fubu  complete their first mega order around  the same time daemon's hip-hop partners  including will smith beyonce and alcoj  were starting to get some notoriety ella  cool j and daymind were actually  childhood friends and the damien was  able to convince cool jay to wear a fubu  hat in a gap commercial cool jay didn't  just stop right there either he was  hired to rap in the commercial and he  snuck in the phrase for us by us in the  rap  c-a-p gritty ready to go for us brothers  on the low g that's forgetting honestly  i'm not sure how gap let this one slip  by but it worked out great for fubu as  their hip-hop partners evolved into  full-fledged celebrities fubu  transitioned from being a small home  business to a national brand in 1998  fubu pulled in 350 million dollars in  sales but damond was just getting  started  fubu was doing better than ever before  damien knew that hip-hop theme was  fickle and that it could disappear just  as fast as it appeared so damon de  cleverly started to diversify as soon as  possible in the late 1990s and early  2000s fubu put hip-hop promotions on the  back burner and started to reinvest  their profits into building an  international audience they primarily  targeted saudi arabia china korea japan  and south africa daemon didn't just  limit the company to streetwear clothing  either in 2000 he launched football  entertainment also known as fubu records  as the name suggests this subsidiary was  focused on producing and releasing music  albums one of their first deals was with  universal records which ended up  generating millions in revenue moving  forward in 2002 daemon embraced internet  with the launch of ytg.com which sold  their various products online all of  these efforts gave fubu a pretty solid  safety net but damon didn't just want to  rely on fubu either so he also started  ventures outside fubu for example daemon  leverages new found fame to start  selling books so far demind has  published four books called display of  power the brand within the power of  broke and rise and grind these  publications have won them the titles of  new york times and wall street journal  best-selling author  aside from publishing books daemon has  also become a public speaker and he  charges 50 to 75 000 per speech demand  has also partnered with several brands  including pitbull miss universe shopify  and most recently audible it's a good  thing damon diversified so heavily as  fubu sales did indeed start dropping  just like he expected from their peak of  350 million dollars in 1998 fubu  declined to 200 million by 1999 and  they've stabilized around there ever  since damon doesn't seem to mind too  much though he knew the drop was coming  and prepared as much as he could also he  had already made more money than he ever  wanted and now he wanted to focus his  efforts on giving back  damon isn't interested in making the  rich richer or even the middle class  richer his primary goal is to help the  poor break out of the poverty cycle he  knows firsthand how impossible it was to  secure a loan and with shark tank  diamond has prioritized giving  opportunity just like samsung textiles  gave him an opportunity one of the best  examples of this was with most bows in  season five of shark tank a young  entrepreneur named moziah pitched his  bow tie making business he asked for a  modest fifty thousand dollars for twenty  percent stake in his business but  instead of offering him the money damon  offered to mentor him for free since  then dementia has helped mozaya secure a  manufacturing partner get into neiman  marcus and even get a seven-figure  licensing deal with the nba they meant  it literally made this kid into a  millionaire for free i don't think it  gets more wholesome than that another  wholesome damage deal was bombas bombas  is a sock company that focuses on  donating socks to homeless shelters the  founders david and randy started the  company after finding out that the most  needed item at homeless shelters was  socks and for every item you purchased  from bombas they donate an item to  homeless organizations it looks like  this message has really resonated with  customers as bombbus is not only damon's  most successful investment but the most  successful investment in shark tank  history grossing a total of 225 million  dollars in lifetime sales shark tank  isn't the only way day many gives back  either in 2015 he co-founded damon  john's success formula which teaches  entrepreneurs how to start and grow  their business and that's emir he was  appointed by president obama to be an  ambassador for underserved entrepreneurs  considering all of this i don't think  there's any doubt that damon is the most  selfless shark on the show  as for damon today he's doing better  than ever before fubu crossed six  billion dollars in annual sales back in  2016 and they're likely in the seven to  eight billion dollar range today if not  even higher  in terms of shark tank investments  daemon has completed 61 deals on air  which comes out to a total of 8.5  million invested considering this i  don't think you'd be too surprised here  that net worth is estimated to be around  350 million dollars unfortunately though  his personal life isn't progressing  nearly as smoothly in april of 2017  damian was diagnosed with stage 2  thyroid cancer he did undergo surgery  and get the cancerous node removed but  it's definitely not something to take  lightly hopefully the cancer never  returns though as the amount is not only  relatively young at 52 but he's a  phenomenal community oriented person and  he would be a massive loss for everybody  do you guys think damon is the best  shark comment that down below  also drop a like if you think that the  other sharks should take a couple of  notes from  and of course consider joining our  discord community to suggest your video  ideas and consider subscribing to see  more questions logically answered but  until then i'm hari and i'll see you  guys on the next one  you

